---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  { question: 'Are ChatGPT ads available to UK advertisers?', answer: 'Yes. On 11 August 2026 OpenAI said ChatGPT Ads had launched in the United Kingdom, and its Ads Manager availability page lists the United Kingdom as available for self-service when the advertising and billed legal entity is based in a listed country. OpenAI reviews each account and ad before it runs. Checked 19 October 2026.' },
  { question: 'Who sees ChatGPT ads?', answer: 'OpenAI says ads may appear for users on the Free and Go plans. Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise and Edu accounts do not have ads, and ads are not shown to accounts identified as belonging to people under 18. Ads are labelled and shown separately from the answer.' },
  { question: 'What ad formats does ChatGPT have?', answer: 'OpenAI says ads can appear below a ChatGPT response as one ad unit that may contain one or several images. It is also testing a multi-image visual ad format that appears while an image is being generated. Product-feed campaigns are a separate paid format in Ads Manager.' },
  { question: 'How are ChatGPT ads priced?', answer: 'OpenAI lets advertisers choose Views (billed per 1,000 impressions), Clicks (billed per valid click) or Conversions (billed per valid click or per 1,000 impressions, never per conversion). OpenAI does not publish typical prices or results in the documents we checked, so any figure quoted elsewhere is not an official one.' },
  { question: 'Can UK finance, health and legal firms advertise in ChatGPT?', answer: 'Mostly no, going by OpenAI ad policy updated 10 September 2026. It says ads for financial services and for health services outside the US are generally prohibited, and ads for legal services outside the US are currently prohibited.' },
  { question: 'Are ChatGPT shopping results paid ads?', answer: 'OpenAI says shopping product results are selected independently and are not ads. Product-feed campaigns are a separate paid format.' },
  { question: 'What should an ecommerce brand prepare?', answer: 'Prepare accurate product data, useful landing pages, a clear purchase event, margin rules and a controlled test plan.' }
];


const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'Article', 'headline': 'ChatGPT Ads in the UK: What OpenAI Has Officially Said', 'description': 'Dated, sourced facts from OpenAI on UK availability, who sees ads, formats and policy, plus what advertisers should do now. Last checked 19 October 2026.', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com/blog/chatgpt-ads', 'datePublished': '2025-07-17', 'dateModified': '2026-10-19', 'author': { '@type': 'Organization', 'name': 'Visible Ads', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com' }, 'publisher': { '@type': 'Organization', 'name': 'Visible Ads', 'url': 'https://visible-ads.com' }, 'image': 'https://visible-ads.com/images/visible-ads-og.png' },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', 'mainEntity': faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer } })) },
    { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', 'itemListElement': [{ '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 1, 'name': 'Home', 'item': 'https://visible-ads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 2, 'name': 'Blog', 'item': 'https://visible-ads.com/blog' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 3, 'name': 'ChatGPT Ads in the UK: What OpenAI Has Officially Said', 'item': 'https://visible-ads.com/blog/chatgpt-ads' }] }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="ChatGPT Ads in the UK: What OpenAI Has Officially Said | Visible Ads" description="Dated facts from OpenAI on ChatGPT Ads in the UK: availability, who sees ads, formats and policy. Last checked 19 October 2026." schema={schema}>
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-navy-light relative overflow-hidden" data-animate>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-5"></div><div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative"><nav class="text-sm text-slate-light mb-8"><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a href="/blog" class="hover:text-white">Blog</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span class="text-white">ChatGPT ads in the UK</span></nav><div class="max-w-3xl"><span class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 bg-electric/20 text-electric-light text-sm font-medium rounded-full mb-6">AI commerce</span><h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white leading-tight mb-6">ChatGPT ads in the UK: what OpenAI has officially said</h1><p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-light leading-relaxed">Every fact below comes from OpenAI's own pages and carries its source and date. Last checked 19 October 2026.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-light"><a href="#changelog" class="underline hover:text-white">See the changelog</a></p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">UK availability, checked 19 October 2026</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">On 11 August 2026 OpenAI said ChatGPT Ads had launched in the United Kingdom, and its Ads Manager availability page lists the United Kingdom as available for self-service. Signing up does not guarantee that an account or campaign will run, because OpenAI reviews ads before they go live and you need billing set up first.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">OpenAI changes these pages often, so this page is re-checked against them and the date above moves when it is. The table below is the full record.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">What OpenAI has officially said</h2><p class="text-gray-700 mb-8 leading-relaxed">Each row is taken from an OpenAI page, with the date OpenAI gives or the date we read it. Wording in quotation marks is OpenAI's own.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">Dated OpenAI statements about ChatGPT Ads, with sources</caption><thead class="bg-navy text-white"><tr><th class="p-4" scope="col">Date</th><th class="p-4" scope="col">What OpenAI says</th><th class="p-4" scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-700"><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">9 Feb 2026</th><td class="p-4">Ad testing started in the United States. The test was for logged-in adult users on the Free and Go plans.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/index/testing-ads-in-chatgpt/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Testing ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">5 May 2026</th><td class="p-4">OpenAI began rolling out a beta self-serve Ads Manager and added cost-per-click bidding. Before that, advertisers bought on a cost-per-thousand-impressions basis.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/index/new-ways-to-buy-chatgpt-ads/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: New ways to buy ChatGPT ads</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">7 May 2026</th><td class="p-4">OpenAI said it planned to expand the ads pilot to the United Kingdom, Mexico, Brazil, Japan and South Korea.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/index/testing-ads-in-chatgpt/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Testing ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">11 Aug 2026</th><td class="p-4">"ChatGPT Ads has now launched in the United Kingdom, Mexico, Brazil, Japan, and South Korea."</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/index/testing-ads-in-chatgpt/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Testing ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">18 and 31 Aug 2026</th><td class="p-4">OpenAI brought ChatGPT Ads to 31 European markets, and said self-service access through Ads Manager reached those markets on 31 August. The page does not say whether the UK is counted in the 31, so this page does not either. It also lists conversion optimisation, geo-targeting, custom audiences, the OpenAI Pixel and the Conversions API as added since the US test began.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-ads-expands-across-europe/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: ChatGPT Ads expands across Europe</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">The Ads Manager availability list shows the United Kingdom as Available for self-service. The legal entity that will advertise and be billed must be based in a listed country.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001245-ads-manager-availability" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Ads Manager availability</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Ads may appear for users on the Free and Go plans. Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise and Edu accounts will not have ads. Ads are not shown to accounts identified as belonging to people under 18, and Temporary Chats do not show ads.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001047-ads-in-chatgpt" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Ads appear below a ChatGPT response as one ad unit that may hold one or several images. OpenAI is also testing a multi-image ad format during image generation. Ads are labelled and shown separately from the response.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001047-ads-in-chatgpt" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Advertisers do not have access to chats, chat history, memories or personal details. They receive aggregated, non-identifying information about how ads perform, such as total views or clicks.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001047-ads-in-chatgpt" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Ads in ChatGPT</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Campaign objectives are Views (pay per 1,000 impressions served), Clicks (pay per valid click) and Conversions (billed per valid click or per 1,000 impressions served). "You do not pay per conversion." The minimum daily budget for accounts billed in pounds is 15 GBP.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001210-create-campaigns-for-chatgpt-ads" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Create campaigns</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Some new self-serve accounts can at first advertise only in their home country.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001210-create-campaigns-for-chatgpt-ads" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Create campaigns</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Read 19 Oct 2026</th><td class="p-4">Country or region, currency and time zone cannot be changed after the ad account is created.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001213" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI Help: Ads Manager account setup</a></td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40 align-top"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy whitespace-nowrap" scope="row">Policy dated 10 Sep 2026</th><td class="p-4">During the initial test period ads are primarily limited to consumer verticals such as lifestyle and household goods, local services, travel and experiences, and digital products or education. Ads for financial services and health services outside the US are generally prohibited, and ads for legal services outside the US are currently prohibited.</td><td class="p-4"><a href="https://openai.com/policies/ad-policies/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Ad policies</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6"><div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">What OpenAI has not published</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Typical CPM or CPC prices for the UK, or any average result. Any figure quoted elsewhere is not an official one.</li><li>How many UK advertisers or users are involved.</li><li>Whether the UK is one of the 31 European markets in the 18 August announcement.</li><li>A UK-only list of ad formats. The formats above are described for ChatGPT generally.</li></ul></div><div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">What advertisers should do now</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Check that the entity that will be billed is UK based and listed as available.</li><li>Confirm your category is allowed. OpenAI generally prohibits finance and health ads outside the US and currently prohibits legal services ads outside the US.</li><li>Set up purchase or lead measurement before spend, so a test can be read.</li><li>Use a capped test and a stop rule, as set out below.</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">A controlled first test</h2><div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6"><div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Before</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Choose a narrow product set, confirm the landing pages and define purchase, refunds and contribution margin. Record the existing sales baseline.</p></div><div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">During</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Use a capped learning budget and watch spend, clicks, observed orders and tracking quality. OpenAI announced CPC bidding and beta self-service tools, but actual account options should be checked in Ads Manager.</p></div><div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">After</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Compare outcomes with the baseline and pre-agreed stop rule. Allow for other channel activity and acknowledge that attribution alone cannot prove additional sales.</p></div></div><p class="mt-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Read our <a href="/blog/multi-channel-attribution/" class="text-electric underline">attribution guide</a> for the measurement limits and the <a href="/blog/ads-in-the-age-of-ai-summaries/" class="text-electric underline">AI summaries guide</a> for the distinction between ads, links and citations. This article covers access and a test decision; the separate commerce readiness page, linked at the foot of this article, explains the review Visible Ads offers.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>What is available in ChatGPT?</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">UK advertisers can apply through Ads Manager when the legal entity that will advertise and be billed is based in a country OpenAI lists as available, and OpenAI reviews each account and ad before it runs. OpenAI says ads are labelled and separate from the answer.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Shopping product results are also separate from ads. OpenAI says those results are selected independently, while product-feed campaigns are a paid format that does not appear organically in ChatGPT conversations. Treat each surface as a different distribution and measurement problem.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">ChatGPT ads vs ChatGPT shopping</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">Comparison of ChatGPT ads and shopping product results</caption><thead class="bg-navy text-white"><tr><th class="p-4">Question</th><th class="p-4">ChatGPT Ads</th><th class="p-4">Shopping product results</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-700"><tr class="border-t"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Commercial model</th><td class="p-4">A paid advertising programme with changing access.</td><td class="p-4">OpenAI describes results as independently selected, not ads.</td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Organic appearance</th><td class="p-4">Product-feed campaigns do not appear organically in conversations.</td><td class="p-4">Product discovery depends on OpenAI's shopping systems and merchant information.</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">First operational question</th><td class="p-4">Is the programme available to this account, market and category?</td><td class="p-4">Are product facts, price, availability and merchant details accurate?</td></tr><tr class="border-t bg-sky-tint/40"><th class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Useful success measure</th><td class="p-4">Incremental commercial outcome against a pre-agreed test rule.</td><td class="p-4">Qualified product discovery and the downstream commerce outcome.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>What ecommerce brands can prepare now</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Ecommerce readiness comes down to four things: the product record, product-page evidence, measurement definitions and commercial guardrails. The <a href="/chatgpt-ads-ecommerce/" class="text-electric underline">ChatGPT commerce readiness page</a> sets out each layer and what a review delivers.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>When should a brand test ChatGPT Ads?</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Test only when OpenAI confirms availability, the catalogue is reliable and the business can measure a commercial result. A brand should not borrow certainty from early access, headlines or a platform metric alone.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The right test starts with a narrow product set, a fixed learning budget and an order-level readout. Use the result to decide whether to extend the test, improve the product record or stop.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2>How Visible Ads assesses commerce readiness</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A commerce-readiness review connects product data, landing pages, tracking and unit economics, and it does not promise access to ChatGPT Ads or any outcome.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">How products become eligible for discovery</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">Shopping results can draw merchant and product metadata from third-party providers or directly from merchants. OpenAI says Shopify product data is integrated through Shopify Catalog, while other merchants can apply for direct product-feed access for shopping.</p><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">That path is separate from Ads Manager product-feed campaigns. Ads Manager feeds make products eligible for paid feed ads during the beta, not organic ChatGPT conversations.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-sky-tint" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">Sources</h2><p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 leading-relaxed">OpenAI changes these products and policies. Confirm current access before committing budget.</p><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001245-ads-manager-availability" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Ads Manager availability</a>, UK listing.</li><li><a href="https://openai.com/index/testing-ads-in-chatgpt/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Testing ads in ChatGPT</a>, launch dates by market and the 11 August 2026 UK update.</li><li><a href="https://openai.com/policies/ad-policies/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Ad policies</a>, permitted categories, updated 10 September 2026.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001210-create-campaigns-for-chatgpt-ads" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Create campaigns for ChatGPT Ads</a>, objectives and billing.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001213" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: Ads Manager account setup</a>, fixed account settings.</li><li><a href="https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-ads-expands-across-europe/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: European expansion</a>, self-service status.</li><li><a href="https://openai.com/index/new-ways-to-buy-chatgpt-ads/" class="text-electric underline">OpenAI: New ways to buy ChatGPT ads</a>, beta self-service and CPC bidding.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en-us/articles/20001047-ads-in-chatgpt" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">OpenAI: Ads in ChatGPT</a>, placement, labels, privacy and reporting.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11128490-improved-shopping-results-from-chatgpt-search" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">OpenAI: Shopping with ChatGPT Search</a>, organic product results.</li><li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001268-create-campaigns-from-product-feeds" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">OpenAI: Create campaigns from product feeds</a>, paid product-feed campaigns.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section id="changelog" class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">Changelog</h2><p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">Last checked 19 October 2026. Next check due by 18 November 2026.</p><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><li><strong>19 October 2026:</strong> every OpenAI source re-read. Added the dated record of OpenAI statements, who sees ads, formats, buying options and the policy limits on finance, health and legal advertising outside the US.</li><li><strong>4 October 2026:</strong> UK Ads Manager availability and European self-service status checked.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="relative py-20 lg:py-28 bg-navy" data-animate><div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-5"></div><div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center"><h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-white mb-6">Assess your ecommerce readiness</h2><p class="text-lg text-slate-light mb-8">Get a practical view of the tracking, catalogue and profit rules behind your next channel test.</p><a href="/chatgpt-ads-ecommerce" class="w-full sm:w-auto inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-cta text-white font-semibold px-10 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-electric transition-colors text-lg">Explore ChatGPT commerce readiness</a></div></section>
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white" data-animate><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="space-y-4">{faqs.map((faq) => <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading font-semibold text-navy">{faq.question}</summary><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
</Layout>
